WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.637
- Good morning believe nation!

00:00:02.637 --> 00:00:05.235
Today's message is stay focused.

00:00:05.235 --> 00:00:06.646
Over to you Victoria Beckham.

00:00:06.646 --> 00:00:08.665
(rooster crow)

00:00:08.665 --> 00:00:11.616
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.616 --> 00:00:14.044
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.044 --> 00:00:17.544
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.709 --> 00:00:22.042
- When I initially started up the brand,

00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:25.172
I didn't put too much pressure on myself,

00:00:25.172 --> 00:00:27.915
I didn't go into this to
prove anything to anybody

00:00:27.915 --> 00:00:29.689
other than myself.

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:33.856
I was very focused, I didn't
try to do everything at once.

00:00:34.789 --> 00:00:38.879
For quite a few seasons I
stuck to just perfecting

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:41.884
the dress, I didn't want
to run before I could walk.

00:00:41.884 --> 00:00:46.619
It's very important to be
focused and do what I was doing

00:00:46.619 --> 00:00:50.786
very, very well and move on
and do more, when my team

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.468
was in the position to do that.

00:00:55.307 --> 00:00:59.127
So I think that it's about
keeping things focused

00:00:59.127 --> 00:01:01.623
and not trying to do too much.

00:01:01.623 --> 00:01:03.239
- I think this is one
of the things that sinks

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:05.072
tons of entrepreneurs.

00:01:06.339 --> 00:01:09.344
So many entrepreneurs that I
know are the creative types,

00:01:09.344 --> 00:01:11.551
right, creative geniuses, amazing.

00:01:11.551 --> 00:01:14.766
And you have this idea, I
love this idea, this is great,

00:01:14.766 --> 00:01:16.793
what an amazing idea, and then
you're off running with it,

00:01:16.793 --> 00:01:20.650
and then poof you meet somebody
or some other idea comes

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.488
to you and then forget this,
I'm going to go over here now,

00:01:23.488 --> 00:01:26.540
and you start working on this
thing and then poof you want

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:27.798
to go this way now.

00:01:27.798 --> 00:01:30.146
You're off on some totally
new thing, and you're sitting

00:01:30.146 --> 00:01:33.948
around with 25 different
projects sitting at 50% done,

00:01:33.948 --> 00:01:36.127
and nothing ever gets to completion.

00:01:36.127 --> 00:01:39.094
That's so many entrepreneurs
because you can't focus on

00:01:39.094 --> 00:01:42.365
one thing at a time, and if
you are that to the extreme,

00:01:42.365 --> 00:01:46.641
if you can only be the
idea generation person,

00:01:46.641 --> 00:01:49.738
and you just can never get
yourself focused, then my

00:01:49.738 --> 00:01:52.060
advice to you isn't force
yourself to be focused because

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.162
you're not going to thrive,
but find somebody to help

00:01:55.162 --> 00:01:56.562
finish these projects.

00:01:56.562 --> 00:01:58.208
Get it to the point where
you're making some money

00:01:58.208 --> 00:02:00.590
with it and somebody can
help partner with you,

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:03.467
who is the super
operations, detail oriented,

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:05.464
focused person, to help
get you through because

00:02:05.464 --> 00:02:07.517
otherwise you're just
going to be sitting there

00:02:07.517 --> 00:02:10.273
on a pile of projects
that never get completed.

00:02:10.273 --> 00:02:11.763
And you're never going to
have the impact of success

00:02:11.763 --> 00:02:13.685
you want as a entrepreneur.

00:02:13.685 --> 00:02:16.825
I'm fortunate enough to have
both, I can be the creative

00:02:16.825 --> 00:02:19.822
and the visionary and go and
do big things, and come up with

00:02:19.822 --> 00:02:21.991
new ideas that haven't happened
before, but I also like

00:02:21.991 --> 00:02:23.381
finishing stuff.

00:02:23.381 --> 00:02:26.762
I like having commitments,
I like scheduling things in,

00:02:26.762 --> 00:02:29.256
and keeping to my schedule.

00:02:29.256 --> 00:02:32.140
What I find the balance
that I strike is most days

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.642
I wake up and I follow my schedule.

00:02:34.642 --> 00:02:37.772
Things have to happen every
week, and this is the schedule

00:02:37.772 --> 00:02:38.708
that I follow.

00:02:38.708 --> 00:02:40.659
Wednesday is my video recording day, I'm

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:43.113
coming to the studio
and I'm filming videos.

00:02:43.113 --> 00:02:45.761
But then on the days that
come where there's some

00:02:45.761 --> 00:02:48.011
crazy idea, I'll go for it,

00:02:50.152 --> 00:02:52.819
I'll start it, I'll work
on it to the expense

00:02:52.819 --> 00:02:54.400
of everything else on my schedule.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.868
I'll move meetings, I'll
switch video day around

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.860
because when I can get into
that zone, I can create

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.343
some amazing stuff.

00:03:01.343 --> 00:03:03.970
But that's not every day,
I don't wake up every day

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:08.872
in the zone, really working
on some new creative idea.

00:03:08.872 --> 00:03:11.170
So I find that that balance
really works for me.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.738
What I've done, is I always
start a project myself.

00:03:14.738 --> 00:03:18.579
Myself, my energy, my time,
my hustle, my drive, and

00:03:18.579 --> 00:03:21.282
then as it builds up I
either get it to the point

00:03:21.282 --> 00:03:24.574
where I can afford to
bring on a team to help me

00:03:24.574 --> 00:03:28.207
because it's making some money,
or I don't, and I drop it.

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:31.664
I kill off more projects
than most people start.

00:03:31.664 --> 00:03:34.099
When I started this YouTube
channel is a great example.

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:36.892
I had a successful business,
I had a website, I still

00:03:36.892 --> 00:03:39.809
have a website, I have a
team of people on my website,

00:03:39.809 --> 00:03:42.454
I decided I'm going to
start a YouTube channel.

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:44.452
I could've taken money from
that business to start the

00:03:44.452 --> 00:03:46.980
channel, to buy the basics,
to buy the gear, and all that

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:50.715
stuff, I started with
zero dollars doing it,

00:03:50.715 --> 00:03:54.101
just my time, borrowed
gear, borrowed equipment,

00:03:54.101 --> 00:03:56.070
I did the editing, I
did the research, I was

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.979
in front of the camera, I did everything.

00:03:57.979 --> 00:04:00.516
I kept my team doing what
they were doing, building that

00:04:00.516 --> 00:04:02.404
business while I went off
and did this crazy thing

00:04:02.404 --> 00:04:03.237
on YouTube.

00:04:03.237 --> 00:04:06.035
Now luckily it worked, and
I built it up and now I've

00:04:06.035 --> 00:04:08.597
built a YouTube team around
it, but a lot of those

00:04:08.597 --> 00:04:11.334
projects that I'll work on
my own, they don't take off.

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:13.523
Most of it is because I
don't, I lose my excitement

00:04:13.523 --> 00:04:16.755
for it, like YouTube could
have been, I made five videos

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:17.772
and then like you know what,
that was a good try, I'm like

00:04:17.772 --> 00:04:20.117
I'm glad I gave it a shot,
it's just I don't enjoy it

00:04:20.117 --> 00:04:22.252
I'm not going to do it, and I cut out.

00:04:22.252 --> 00:04:25.086
And so I think it's super
important that you understand

00:04:25.086 --> 00:04:27.640
the personality type that
you are, you have that

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:31.924
self awareness to say,
either I can be more focused

00:04:31.924 --> 00:04:35.917
and I need to pick the project
that I'm going to work on,

00:04:35.917 --> 00:04:36.750
right?

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.138
This is something I'm doing
with trying to dance salsa.

00:04:39.138 --> 00:04:42.194
This business right here, and
Alex, I gave him ten options

00:04:42.194 --> 00:04:43.177
when we sat down.

00:04:43.177 --> 00:04:45.328
Here are the ten ways we
can grow our business.

00:04:45.328 --> 00:04:47.725
Ten different ways, we
can't do all of them because

00:04:47.725 --> 00:04:49.120
if we try to do all of
them, we're going to suck

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.732
at everything, we're going
to have a whole bunch of

00:04:50.732 --> 00:04:52.091
50% projects.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:55.856
This one we have to do, you
pick one of the other nine.

00:04:55.856 --> 00:05:00.487
He picked one, and every time
it's tempting to come back

00:05:00.487 --> 00:05:02.703
and say oooh, ooh here's an idea.

00:05:02.703 --> 00:05:04.513
I saw this video that somebody
put out, what if we did

00:05:04.513 --> 00:05:07.831
like this thing way over here, no, focus!

00:05:07.831 --> 00:05:11.382
Forget that, yes it can work,
but it has to be done well.

00:05:11.382 --> 00:05:14.323
Focus, these two things, that's
what we're doing, that's it.

00:05:14.323 --> 00:05:17.558
Don't worry about anything
else, and if you don't have

00:05:17.558 --> 00:05:19.928
the discipline to put that
on yourself, and it's not the

00:05:19.928 --> 00:05:22.569
skill set that you want
to build and develop then

00:05:22.569 --> 00:05:24.422
you need to have somebody
come on and help you.

00:05:24.422 --> 00:05:26.695
You need to have somebody
that you can hand projects

00:05:26.695 --> 00:05:27.936
off to and they can run with it.

00:05:27.936 --> 00:05:30.114
And you can take it far
enough to get to the point

00:05:30.114 --> 00:05:31.636
where you can make some money with it,

00:05:31.636 --> 00:05:34.701
and they can run with it and
help you build the business,

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:37.159
while you move onto the next
project, then the next project,

00:05:37.159 --> 00:05:38.367
and the next project.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:41.303
You need to have that skill
somewhere in your arsenal,

00:05:41.303 --> 00:05:43.310
either you develop it
yourself or you bring somebody

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:45.060
on to help you, otherwise
you're not going to have

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.736
success as an entrepreneur.

00:05:46.736 --> 00:05:49.742
So the question of the day
today is, are you focused

00:05:49.742 --> 00:05:53.105
enough at finishing the
projects that you start?

00:05:53.105 --> 00:05:55.139
Leave in the comments below I'm going

00:05:55.139 --> 00:05:56.463
to join in the discussion.

00:05:56.463 --> 00:05:58.742
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Steve Saunders from

00:05:58.742 --> 00:06:00.416
stevesaunders.info.

00:06:00.416 --> 00:06:03.068
Steve, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book.

00:06:03.068 --> 00:06:06.412
Your One Word, I really,
really, really appreciate it.

00:06:06.412 --> 00:06:09.084
Thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:06:09.084 --> 00:06:11.221
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:06:11.221 --> 00:06:13.894
and whatever your one word
is and I'll see you again

00:06:13.894 --> 00:06:17.269
tomorrow morning for
another shot of entpresso.

00:06:17.269 --> 00:06:19.544
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:19.544 --> 00:06:23.312
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:06:23.312 --> 00:06:25.635
- So as a special bonus
for you guys, I'm adding

00:06:25.635 --> 00:06:28.169
some extra clips around
staying focused that I hope

00:06:28.169 --> 00:06:30.165
you will enjoy and will help.

00:06:30.165 --> 00:06:34.878
- How do you prepare
yourself to be so focused,

00:06:34.878 --> 00:06:37.711
to handle all this massive stress?

00:06:40.224 --> 00:06:44.524
- Really it's trying
to just remain focused

00:06:44.524 --> 00:06:47.426
on the job at hand and then the task.

00:06:47.426 --> 00:06:50.266
My goal this weekend is to win this race.

00:06:50.266 --> 00:06:54.067
All the other stuff is all just
noise, and I guess it's just

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:57.642
through experience being
able to silence all that

00:06:57.642 --> 00:07:00.473
and stay focused on what's
the most important thing.

00:07:00.473 --> 00:07:04.055
So don't be distracted by
all the media, all the camers

00:07:04.055 --> 00:07:08.487
tomorrow there's so many
interviews, mostly with

00:07:08.487 --> 00:07:11.088
the same people that we always
have, so I've been talking

00:07:11.088 --> 00:07:14.632
to these guys for ten
years, but are often asking

00:07:14.632 --> 00:07:17.874
the same question that
they ask me two weeks ago.

00:07:17.874 --> 00:07:19.904
But obviously they have
something more to talk

00:07:19.904 --> 00:07:22.513
about this weekend because
the last race was terrible.

00:07:22.513 --> 00:07:26.680
But I think really it's
trying to compartmentalize

00:07:27.649 --> 00:07:32.099
really that stuff put over
here, put it in a box, and then

00:07:32.099 --> 00:07:35.363
keep the energy and your
focus on the one thing

00:07:35.363 --> 00:07:36.529
that matters most.

00:07:36.529 --> 00:07:38.162
All of that other stuff does
not matter, what matters is

00:07:38.162 --> 00:07:42.482
me and this team, how are
we going to get from Friday,

00:07:42.482 --> 00:07:45.539
or Thursday this week
for example, to Sunday

00:07:45.539 --> 00:07:47.871
standing on top of that podium.

00:07:47.871 --> 00:07:52.059
It's sleep, it's what I eat,
it's what I spend my time

00:07:52.059 --> 00:07:54.594
doing, making sure I get to bed early.

00:07:54.594 --> 00:07:57.601
All these different
things that add up to it.

00:07:57.601 --> 00:08:00.091
And sometimes you do it all
perfect, and it doesn't go well,

00:08:00.091 --> 00:08:03.960
but that's life, and you just
hope that in doing all the

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.538
right things, but it's also
trying to find a balance,

00:08:07.538 --> 00:08:10.304
you need to enjoy life as well.

00:08:10.304 --> 00:08:13.471
At some stage I'm going,
my career will be over, and

00:08:13.471 --> 00:08:14.679
I want to look back and say

00:08:14.679 --> 00:08:16.754
I enjoyed absolutely everything,

00:08:16.754 --> 00:08:20.082
every moment in the car,
every moment out of it.

00:08:20.082 --> 00:08:22.880
- Well when you're doing a tv
show, every day is a different

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:25.520
day in the sense that it's never the same.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.563
And you might be shooting
two scenes, you might have

00:08:27.563 --> 00:08:31.269
one scene, you might have
five scenes, so your level

00:08:31.269 --> 00:08:34.519
of preparation is different every time.

00:08:35.629 --> 00:08:39.143
Generally I'm up early, I
exercise, I run, I do whatever

00:08:39.143 --> 00:08:41.764
it is I'm doing in terms
of my physical life other

00:08:41.764 --> 00:08:45.294
than playing tennis, which
I stack up during the

00:08:45.294 --> 00:08:48.564
course of a week, quite
a lot of, if I can.

00:08:48.564 --> 00:08:51.557
And get to set, depending
on your call time but

00:08:51.557 --> 00:08:53.927
very often it's very early.

00:08:53.927 --> 00:08:58.780
And then you try to be
there and be alert and awake

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:02.410
and alive and ready to
go every hour of the day.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.622
And if you work twelve
hours then you have to be

00:09:04.622 --> 00:09:07.205
alert every one of those hours.

00:09:08.912 --> 00:09:12.775
It's an important thing to stay focused.

00:09:12.775 --> 00:09:16.468
- It wasn't conscious on my
part to have another script

00:09:16.468 --> 00:09:21.259
sort of ready to go by the
time we went to film festivals

00:09:21.259 --> 00:09:25.267
with Following, while we were
finishing up the cut on it

00:09:25.267 --> 00:09:28.695
and doing very long,
slow technical finishing,

00:09:28.695 --> 00:09:31.031
which when you have no money
it takes forever because

00:09:31.031 --> 00:09:34.909
you're still waiting for
the lab to run the 16mm bath

00:09:34.909 --> 00:09:38.912
or whatever it is, in that
time I was putting together

00:09:38.912 --> 00:09:43.079
a script for Memento so also
in the time it took to get

00:09:44.246 --> 00:09:46.439
Following noticed on the
festival circuit so we could

00:09:46.439 --> 00:09:48.515
get out there, I had
actually finished the script.

00:09:48.515 --> 00:09:52.295
In retrospect, it was a
massive advantage because I was

00:09:52.295 --> 00:09:55.463
able to say okay you like
that film, this is what I want

00:09:55.463 --> 00:09:58.905
to do next because in your
best case scenario of what

00:09:58.905 --> 00:10:01.936
can happen to you with putting
a film out there and getting

00:10:01.936 --> 00:10:06.628
distribution for example, you
are then asked the question

00:10:06.628 --> 00:10:08.908
okay what do you want to do
next, and if you have an answer

00:10:08.908 --> 00:10:13.194
you can use that very short
window of interest that you

00:10:13.194 --> 00:10:15.971
get from people in what you've done.

00:10:15.971 --> 00:10:19.587
But I will say that I think
that was purely an accident,

00:10:19.587 --> 00:10:23.754
and I think that if you were
to try and plan to write

00:10:26.507 --> 00:10:29.719
another script while
you are finishing a film

00:10:29.719 --> 00:10:32.168
you really risk taking
your focus off the project

00:10:32.168 --> 00:10:33.419
that you're doing.

00:10:33.419 --> 00:10:37.432
And I think that it's most
important to just throw yourself

00:10:37.432 --> 00:10:41.360
into just putting everything
into the project you're working

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:44.840
on and that's something
I've always done since.

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:48.302
If you can then because
quite often there is a period

00:10:48.302 --> 00:10:50.844
between finishing a project
and actually people seeing it

00:10:50.844 --> 00:10:52.488
or actually people responding to it.

00:10:52.488 --> 00:10:54.534
If you can try instead of going
on holiday for six months,

00:10:54.534 --> 00:10:57.196
you can use that period
to try and figure out what

00:10:57.196 --> 00:10:59.996
you would do next if someone
gave you the opportunity.

00:10:59.996 --> 00:11:03.340
Then you're going to give
yourself a huge advantage.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:06.370
- Obstacles really don't matter.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:10.537
They really just don't, no
more than where you come from,

00:11:12.581 --> 00:11:16.646
what you had, what you
have, what you didn't have,

00:11:16.646 --> 00:11:19.936
all that stuff becomes so what.

00:11:19.936 --> 00:11:22.019
People that are concerned

00:11:25.927 --> 00:11:29.427
with results and the person that's working

00:11:30.354 --> 00:11:34.852
with their mind fixed on the
end result of being success

00:11:34.852 --> 00:11:38.435
are a lot less concerned
about the problems

00:11:41.306 --> 00:11:45.441
and they're more willing
to explore solutions,

00:11:45.441 --> 00:11:47.774
and if need be, create them.

00:11:49.029 --> 00:11:52.779
That is probably the
best use of your energy.

00:11:55.549 --> 00:12:00.141
Arnold Schwarzenegger was said
to have once give a seminar

00:12:00.141 --> 00:12:05.005
somewhere, I think they
referenced it in the, either

00:12:05.005 --> 00:12:09.172
the book The Education Of A
Bodybuilder or the encyclopedia

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:15.584
Arnold Schwarzenegger's
Encyclopeica of Bodybuilding,

00:12:15.584 --> 00:12:19.751
one time giving a seminar it
was said that he talked about

00:12:23.084 --> 00:12:27.842
focusing on his goal and
how the only time you can

00:12:27.842 --> 00:12:32.009
begin to really assess the
enormity of an obstacle was

00:12:35.838 --> 00:12:39.588
to have to first take
your eye off your goal.

00:12:43.377 --> 00:12:45.554
That's the end of my Arnold
Schwarzenegger quote.

00:12:45.554 --> 00:12:49.304
But I guess in recalling
that at this moment,

00:12:51.802 --> 00:12:55.885
what I realize is if I'm
a NFL outside linebacker

00:12:59.625 --> 00:13:02.313
looking to try to put a
sack on the quarterback

00:13:02.313 --> 00:13:04.063
of the opposing team,

00:13:06.648 --> 00:13:10.815
if I am looking at the size
of the lineman in front of me,

00:13:13.941 --> 00:13:17.531
looking to stop me, the
defenders looking to stop me,

00:13:17.531 --> 00:13:20.951
from getting to the quarterback,
if I start taking into

00:13:20.951 --> 00:13:24.198
account, wow, how big is
his hands, and how much does

00:13:24.198 --> 00:13:28.365
this guy weigh, and man,
look at the size of his neck,

00:13:29.528 --> 00:13:33.140
chances are in order to make
all of those assessments,

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:36.450
I can't be looking at the
quarterback behind him anymore.

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:41.314
And if my responsibility in
this play, was to put pressure

00:13:41.314 --> 00:13:45.245
on the quarterback and even
better, put my hands on the

00:13:45.245 --> 00:13:49.823
quarterback, cause a fumble
or stop the play, then I'm

00:13:49.823 --> 00:13:53.420
going to be rendered
ineffective, not by anything the

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:56.759
lineman has done, but because
I have now taken my eye

00:13:56.759 --> 00:14:01.674
off the goal in order to
assess the size and weight

00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:04.257
of the obstacle in front of me.

00:14:06.077 --> 00:14:10.244
Successful people I imagine
have to worry less about

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:15.092
what the size of the obstacles
are, the finances or the

00:14:15.092 --> 00:14:19.259
lack thereof and all the
other things that we can say

00:14:20.887 --> 00:14:25.054
represent the size and the
weight of the opposition,

00:14:27.446 --> 00:14:29.720
and what the successful
person is going to aim to do,

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:33.887
what all of us would like to
be successful would probably

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:40.223
want to adopt as part of
our philosophy, would be

00:14:43.689 --> 00:14:45.664
to worry less about the obstacles

00:14:45.664 --> 00:14:48.414
and fix our thoughts on the goal.

